#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:4
msgid ""
"The plot-methods of FElupe, e.g. :meth:`Mesh.plot() <felupe.Mesh.plot>`, "
":meth:`FieldContainer.plot() <felupe.FieldContainer.plot>` or "
":meth:`SolidBody.plot() <felupe.SolidBody.plot>`, and the plots of the "
"decorations of a model, e.g. of boundary conditions, point loads or rigid "
"contact surfaces, are drawn by a plotting backend. The current plotting "
"backend is selected by its name with :func:`~felupe.set_plotting_backend` "
"and returned by :func:`~felupe.get_plotting_backend`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:19
msgid ""
"The arguments of the plot-methods are the same for all plotting backends, "
"e.g. the name and the component of the scalars, the scale ``factor`` of the "
"deformation, the ``view`` or ``nonlinear_subdivision`` for curved faces of "
"quadratic cells. A plot-method returns the plotter of the plotting backend. "
"Options which are specific to PyVista, e.g. a ``theme``, raise a warning "
"once in the other plotting backends and they are ignored."
