#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:77
msgid "PyVista"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:79
msgid ""
"The plotting backend ``\"pyvista\"`` is the default plotting backend. A "
"plot-method returns a :class:`pyvista.Plotter`, i.e. the plot may be "
"customized by the API of PyVista before it is shown. Screenshots are taken "
"by an off-screen plotter. The plots of finite elements and regions, e.g. of "
"a :class:`~felupe.Hexahedron` or of a :class:`~felupe.RegionHexahedron`, are"
" only supported by this plotting backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:102
msgid "WebGL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:104
msgid ""
"The plotting backend ``\"webgl\"`` draws the plots by a dependency-free "
"WebGL viewer in the web browser, without PyVista. The plotter, a "
":class:`~felupe.view.WebGLPlotter`, is shown by "
":meth:`~felupe.view.WebGLPlotter.show`: in a notebook, the self-contained "
"HTML page of the viewer is shown in the output of the cell, otherwise it is "
"opened in the web browser. The page works offline and it may be written to a"
" file by :meth:`~felupe.view.WebGLPlotter.export_html`, e.g. to share a "
"model. Drag to rotate, shift-drag to pan, scroll to zoom and double-click to"
" reset the view. The live dashboard of a job, "
":class:`~felupe.DashboardWidgetPlugin`, uses the same viewer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:121
msgid ""
"In a notebook, :meth:`~felupe.view.WebGLPlotter.widget` returns a Jupyter "
"widget of the viewer, e.g. for a layout of widgets. This requires the "
"optional dependency ``anywidget`` (``pip install felupe[web]``). Screenshots"
" are not supported by this plotting backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:135
msgid "Matplotlib"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:137
msgid ""
"The plotting backend ``\"matplotlib\"`` draws the plots on the axes of a "
"figure of matplotlib, without PyVista. The plotter, a "
":class:`~felupe.view.MatplotlibPlotter`, has the attributes ``figure`` and "
"``ax``, e.g. to add a title, and it is shown by ``show()``: by pyplot in a "
"window or as image in the output of a cell of a notebook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:171
msgid ""
"The screenshots are taken off-screen, i.e. without a display and without a "
"figure of pyplot. The format of the file is given by the suffix of the "
"filename, i.e. a raster format (PNG) or a vector format (PDF, SVG or EPS). A"
" screenshot in a vector format contains a polygon for each visible face of "
"the model (with its edges), i.e. it stays sharp at any zoom level, e.g. in a"
" publication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:182
msgid ""
"Axes of matplotlib are accepted as plotter, i.e. a model may be drawn "
"together with other plots in one figure, e.g. with its force-displacement "
"curve. The scene on given axes is drawn whenever an object is added, i.e. "
"the figure is saved as usual by :meth:`fig.savefig() "
"<matplotlib.figure.Figure.savefig>`, e.g. in a vector format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:207
msgid ""
"The faces are drawn as polygons with a flat color each, in the order of "
"their depths (painter's algorithm), and the faces on the back of closed "
"surfaces are not drawn. Hence, faces which intersect each other, e.g. at a "
"contact, may be drawn in a wrong order. The edges of the faces are "
"subdivided by ``nonlinear_subdivision=k`` into ``order * 2 ** (k - 1)`` "
"segments, also of linear cells, i.e. the colors of point-data are smoother "
"for ``k > 1``. Planar models are drawn by a parallel projection, other "
"models by a perspective projection, unless it is changed by "
"``plotter.enable_parallel_projection()``. For very large models, the model "
"may be rasterized in vector formats by ``plotter.rasterized = True``, while "
"the scalar bars, the legend and the text stay vector graphics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:225
msgid "Combine Plots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:227
msgid ""
"The plotter of a plot-method is passed to other plot-methods by the argument"
" ``plotter``, e.g. to draw the boundary conditions or a point load on top of"
" the deformed model. A given plotter is always drawn by its own plotting "
"backend, i.e. a :class:`pyvista.Plotter` is drawn by PyVista, independent of"
" the current plotting backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:240
msgid "Custom Plotting Backends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plotting.rst:242
msgid ""
"A custom plotting backend is a subclass of "
":class:`~felupe.view.PlottingBackend`. It implements the methods "
"``is_plotter(plotter)``, ``prepare_plotter(plotter=None, **kwargs)`` and "
"``add_view(plotter, scene, **kwargs)``. The primitives of the decorations, "
"e.g. ``add_points()``, ``add_lines()``, ``add_arrows()``, ``add_shape()`` "
"and ``add_legend()``, and ``screenshot()`` are optional. The scenes provide "
"their points, cells, cell type, point- and cell-data as arrays, i.e. a "
"plotting backend doesn't depend on PyVista. A plotting backend is registered"
" by a name with :func:`~felupe.view.register_plotting_backend`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:2
msgid "Use Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:4
msgid ""
"Plugins extend the evaluation of a :class:`~felupe.Job`. A plugin provides "
"methods with the names of events, called hooks, e.g. before or after each "
"step, each substep or each iteration of the Newton-Raphson method. Plugins "
"record results, write files, show the progress or even change the "
"evaluation, e.g. by a line search or by a cutback of failed substeps. The "
"plugins are passed as a list to the job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:29
msgid "Built-in Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:31
msgid ""
"FElupe ships with the following plugins. The progress and the XDMF result "
"file are enabled by the arguments of :meth:`~felupe.Job.evaluate`, all other"
" plugins are passed to the job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:38
msgid "Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:39
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:41
msgid ":class:`~felupe.ProgressPlugin`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:42
msgid ""
"Shows a progress bar or a text-based output of the Newton-Raphson "
"iterations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:43
msgid "``felupe[progress]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:44
msgid ":class:`~felupe.XDMFWriterPlugin`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:45
msgid "Writes the results of all substeps to a XDMF time series file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../felupe/docs/howto/plugins.rst:46
msgid "``felupe[io]``"
msgstr ""

